diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -250,6 +250,13 @@
 
 It also works when the charset has been detected in `charsetSentinel` mode.
 
+To keep only some top-level keys, pass them as `allowedKeys`. Every other parameter is dropped before it is parsed, so a listed key's nested keys are kept and an unlisted key never reaches the result:
+
+```javascript
+var only = qs.parse('a=1&b[c]=2&d=3', { allowedKeys: ['a', 'b'] });
+assert.deepEqual(only, { a: '1', b: { c: '2' } });
+```
+
 ### Parsing Arrays
 
 **qs** can also parse arrays using a similar `[]` notation:
